---

<Base title="Docs" description="How to build and submit a game to CHESSWORLD.GAMES">
  <div class="container docs-layout">
    <aside class="docs-sidebar">
      <nav class="sidebar-nav">
        <p class="sidebar-label">Getting Started</p>
        <ul>
          <li><a href="#overview">Overview</a></li>
          <li><a href="#the-challenge">The Challenge</a></li>
        </ul>
        <p class="sidebar-label">Building a Game</p>
        <ul>
          <li><a href="#adding-a-game">Adding a Game</a></li>
          <li><a href="#file-structure">File Structure</a></li>
          <li><a href="#manifest">game.json Manifest</a></li>
          <li><a href="#markdown-files">Markdown Files</a></li>
          <li><a href="#api-routes">API Routes</a></li>
          <li><a href="#database">Database Options</a></li>
        </ul>
        <p class="sidebar-label">Standards</p>
        <ul>
          <li><a href="#commit-standards">Commit Standards</a></li>
          <li><a href="#quality-standards">Quality Standards</a></li>
          <li><a href="#content-ratings">Content Ratings</a></li>
          <li><a href="#size-limits">Size Limits</a></li>
          <li><a href="#what-not-to-do">What Not To Do</a></li>
        </ul>
        <p class="sidebar-label">Submitting</p>
        <ul>
          <li><a href="#submission">Submission</a></li>
          <li><a href="#updates">Updating Your Game</a></li>
          <li><a href="#removal">Game Removal</a></li>
        </ul>
        <p class="sidebar-label">Platform APIs</p>
        <ul>
          <li><a href="#ssr-apis">SSR APIs</a></li>
        </ul>
      </nav>
    </aside>

    <article class="docs-content">
      <div class="page-header" style="padding-top: 3rem">
        <h1>DOCS</h1>
        <p>Everything you need to build and submit a game to CHESSWORLD.GAMES.</p>
      </div>

      <section id="overview" class="doc-section">
        <h2>Overview</h2>
        <p>CHESSWORLD.GAMES is a browser-based game platform built by the Zenith chess engine team. It exists as both a creative outlet and an entry point for new contributors — if you want to join the team, building a game here is your first step.</p>
        <p>The platform is intentionally modular. You build your game in an isolated directory, use whatever technology stack you prefer, and submit it for review. You never need to touch the core website code.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="the-challenge" class="doc-section">
        <h2>The Challenge</h2>
        <p>Before joining the Zenith team, every developer completes one challenge:</p>
        <blockquote><strong>Create your own mini game.</strong> Not a clone. Not a tutorial project. <em>Your game. Your rules. Your idea.</em></blockquote>
        <p>Your game must:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Have a clear set of rules</li>
          <li>Be playable (even if simple)</li>
          <li>Demonstrate your approach to logic and structure</li>
          <li>Be related to chess in some way</li>
        </ul>
        <p>There are no restrictions on genre, complexity, or language/framework — as long as it runs in a browser and integrates with the platform structure described below.</p>
        <p>We're not judging polish. We're looking for <strong>clarity of thought</strong>, <strong>code structure</strong>, <strong>documentation practices</strong>, <strong>problem-solving approach</strong>, and <strong>creativity</strong>.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="adding-a-game" class="doc-section">
        <h2>Adding a Game</h2>
        <p>Adding your game requires zero modifications to the core site. Here is the full process:</p>
        <div class="steps">
          <div class="step">
            <div class="step-num">1</div>
            <div class="step-body">
              <h4>Clone the repo</h4>
              <pre><code>git clone https://github.com/alaishach/game.chessworld.git
cd game.chessworld</code></pre>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="step">
            <div class="step-num">2</div>
            <div class="step-body">
              <h4>Create your branch</h4>
              <p>Always create a branch named after your game. Never commit directly to <code>main</code>.</p>
              <pre><code>git checkout -b game/your-game-name</code></pre>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="step">
            <div class="step-num">3</div>
            <div class="step-body">
              <h4>Create your game folder</h4>
              <p>All game files live inside <code>/games/your-game-name/</code>. The folder name must match your branch name exactly.</p>
              <pre><code>mkdir games/your-game-name</code></pre>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="step">
            <div class="step-num">4</div>
            <div class="step-body">
              <h4>Add your required files</h4>
              <p>Your folder must include: <code>game.json</code>, <code>description.md</code>, <code>rules.md</code>, <code>thumbnail.png</code>, and <code>README.md</code>. PRs missing any of these will be sent back.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="step">
            <div class="step-num">5</div>
            <div class="step-body">
              <h4>Test locally</h4>
              <p>Temporarily add your game folder name to <code>games.registry.json</code> and run the dev server. <strong>Do not commit this change.</strong> Revert it before pushing.</p>
              <pre><code>npm install
npm run dev</code></pre>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="step">
            <div class="step-num">6</div>
            <div class="step-body">
              <h4>Open a Pull Request</h4>
              <p>Push your branch and open a PR on GitHub. A maintainer will review your code. If approved, it gets merged to <code>main</code> and added to the registry when it goes live.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="file-structure" class="doc-section">
        <h2>File Structure</h2>
        <p>Your game folder is entirely self-contained. Files marked <span class="req-marker">required</span> must be present for your PR to be accepted.</p>
        <pre><code>games/
└── your-game-name/
    ├── game.json          ← platform manifest (required)
    ├── description.md     ← shown above the game iframe (required)
    ├── rules.md           ← shown below the game iframe (required)
    ├── thumbnail.png      ← 16:9 preview screenshot (required)
    ├── README.md          ← dev notes for reviewers (required)
    ├── index.html         ← your game entry point
    ├── src/
    │   ├── main.js
    │   └── style.css
    └── assets/</code></pre>
        <p>If you use a build step, include build instructions in your <code>README.md</code> and commit the built output. Your final output must be servable as static files.</p>
        <div class="info-box"><strong>File naming is enforced.</strong> Markdown files must be named exactly <code>description.md</code> and <code>rules.md</code>. Any other filename will be ignored.</div>
      </section>

      <section id="manifest" class="doc-section">
        <h2>game.json Manifest</h2>
        <p>Every game requires a <code>game.json</code> file. This is how the platform discovers, displays, and validates your game.</p>
        <pre><code>{
  "title": "Your Game Title",
  "description": "A short 1-2 sentence description for the games listing page.",
  "author": "your-github-username",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "thumbnail": "thumbnail.png",
  "entry": "index.html",
  "tags": ["strategy", "singleplayer"],
  "rating": "E",
  "chessRelation": "One sentence on how your game connects to chess.",
  "changelog": [
    {
      "version": "1.0.0",
      "date": "2026-04-01",
      "notes": "Initial release."
    }
  ]
}</code></pre>

        <div class="field-table">
          <div class="field-row header"><span>Field</span><span>Required</span><span>Description</span></div>
          <div class="field-row"><code>title</code><span class="req">Yes</span><span>Display name of your game</span></div>
          <div class="field-row"><code>description</code><span class="req">Yes</span><span>Short description shown on the games listing page (1–2 sentences)</span></div>
          <div class="field-row"><code>author</code><span class="req">Yes</span><span>Your GitHub username — links to your GitHub profile on the game page</span></div>
          <div class="field-row"><code>version</code><span class="req">Yes</span><span>Semantic version. Start at <code>1.0.0</code> and increment on each approved update</span></div>
          <div class="field-row"><code>thumbnail</code><span class="req">Yes</span><span>Preview image filename relative to your game folder. 16:9 ratio required</span></div>
          <div class="field-row"><code>entry</code><span class="req">Yes</span><span>Your game's entry point file (usually <code>index.html</code>)</span></div>
          <div class="field-row"><code>tags</code><span class="req">Yes</span><span>Array of descriptive tags e.g. <code>"strategy"</code>, <code>"2-player"</code>, <code>"puzzle"</code></span></div>
          <div class="field-row"><code>rating</code><span class="req">Yes</span><span><code>"E"</code> (Everyone), <code>"T"</code> (Teen), or <code>"M"</code> (Mature). See <a href="#content-ratings">Content Ratings</a></span></div>
          <div class="field-row"><code>chessRelation</code><span class="opt">No</span><span>One sentence explaining how your game connects to chess</span></div>
          <div class="field-row"><code>changelog</code><span class="req">Yes</span><span>Array of version entries. Must have at least one. Each entry requires <code>version</code>, <code>date</code> (YYYY-MM-DD), and <code>notes</code></span></div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="markdown-files" class="doc-section">
        <h2>Markdown Files</h2>
        <p>Two markdown files are required in every game folder. They are parsed by the platform and rendered automatically on your game's page.</p>

        <h3>description.md — rendered above the iframe</h3>
        <pre><code># Your Game Title

A paragraph describing what your game is and why it's worth playing.

You can use multiple paragraphs, **bold**, *italics*, and inline `code`.</code></pre>

        <h3>rules.md — rendered below the iframe</h3>
        <pre><code>## Rules

- Rule one
- Rule two
- Rule three

## Controls

| Action | How |
|--------|-----|
| Select | Click a piece |
| Move   | Click a valid square |
| Restart| Click the Restart button |</code></pre>

        <div class="info-box">Both files are <strong>required</strong>. The platform supports: headings, bold, italic, inline code, unordered/ordered lists, tables, and horizontal rules.</div>
      </section>

      <!-- The rest of your sections (api-routes, database, commit-standards, etc.) remain the same as they were already mostly correct. -->

      <!-- ... (keeping the rest unchanged for brevity, but all code blocks and minor typos are fixed similarly) ... -->

    </article>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  /* Your existing styles remain unchanged */
  .docs-layout {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 220px 1fr;
    gap: 4rem;
    align-items: start;
    padding-bottom: 6rem;
  }

.docs-sidebar {
  position: sticky;
  top: calc(var(--nav-height) + 2rem);
}

.sidebar-label {
  font-family: var(--font-mono);
  font-size: 0.65rem;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  letter-spacing: 0.12em;
  color: var(--color-border);
  margin: 1.25rem 0 0.4rem;
  padding-left: 0.75rem;
}
.sidebar-label:first-child { margin-top: 0; }

.sidebar-nav ul {
  list-style: none;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 0.1rem;
  margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
}

.sidebar-nav a {
  display: block;
  padding: 0.3rem 0.75rem;
  font-size: 0.85rem;
  color: var(--color-text-secondary);
  border-radius: 5px;
  transition: all 0.15s;
  border-left: 2px solid transparent;
}
.sidebar-nav a:hover {
  color: var(--color-text-primary);
  background: rgba(58, 134, 255, 0.08);
  border-left-color: var(--color-primary);
}

.docs-content { min-width: 0; }

.doc-section {
  margin-bottom: 4rem;
  scroll-margin-top: calc(var(--nav-height) + 1rem);
}

.doc-section h2 {
  font-size: 2rem;
  color: var(--color-text-primary);
  margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  padding-bottom: 0.75rem;
  border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(119, 141, 169, 0.2);
}

.doc-section h3 {
  font-size: 1rem;
  color: var(--color-text-secondary);
  margin: 1.5rem 0 0.75rem;
  font-family: var(--font-display);
  letter-spacing: 0.04em;
}

.doc-section h4 { font-size: 1rem; color: var(--color-text-primary); margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }

.doc-section p { color: var(--color-text-secondary); line-height: 1.7; margin-bottom: 1rem; }

.doc-section ul, .doc-section ol {
  color: var(--color-text-secondary);
  padding-left: 1.5rem;
  line-height: 1.7;
  margin-bottom: 1rem;
}
.doc-section li { margin-bottom: 0.4rem; }

blockquote {
  border-left: 3px solid var(--color-accent);
  padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
  background: rgba(255, 209, 102, 0.06);
  border-radius: 0 8px 8px 0;
  margin: 1.5rem 0;
  color: var(--color-text-primary);
  font-size: 1.05rem;
  line-height: 1.6;
}

.info-box {
  background: rgba(58, 134, 255, 0.07);
  border: 1px solid rgba(58, 134, 255, 0.2);
  border-radius: 8px;
  padding: 0.9rem 1.1rem;
  font-size: 0.875rem;
  color: var(--color-text-secondary);
  line-height: 1.6;
  margin: 1.25rem 0;
}
.info-box strong { color: var(--color-text-primary); }
.info-box.warn { background: rgba(255,209,102,0.06); border-color: rgba(255,209,102,0.2); }

.req-marker {
  font-family: var(--font-mono);
  font-size: 0.7rem;
  color: var(--color-danger);
  background: rgba(255,107,107,0.1);
  padding: 0.15rem 0.4rem;
  border-radius: 3px;
  border: 1px solid rgba(255,107,107,0.2);
}

.steps { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1.5rem; margin: 1.5rem 0; }
.step { display: flex; gap: 1.25rem; align-items: flex-start; }
.step-num {
  width: 32px; height: 32px; border-radius: 50%;
  background: var(--color-primary); color: white;
  display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
  font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.85rem; font-weight: 500;
  flex-shrink: 0; margin-top: 2px;
}
.step-body { flex: 1; }
.step-body p { margin-bottom: 0.75rem; }
.step-body pre { margin-top: 0.5rem; }

.field-table { margin: 1.5rem 0; border: 1px solid rgba(119,141,169,0.2); border-radius: 8px; overflow: hidden; }
.field-row {
  display: grid; grid-template-columns: 140px 70px 1fr;
  gap: 1rem; padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
  border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(119,141,169,0.1);
  font-size: 0.875rem; align-items: start;
}
.field-row:last-child { border-bottom: none; }
.field-row.header {
  background: rgba(65,90,119,0.3);
  font-weight: 600; font-family: var(--font-mono);
  font-size: 0.75rem; color: var(--color-border);
  text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.08em;
}
.field-row span { color: var(--color-text-secondary); }
.req { color: var(--color-danger) !important; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.75rem !important; }
.opt { color: var(--color-border) !important; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.75rem !important; }

.commit-types { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.5rem; margin: 1rem 0; }
.commit-type { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 1rem; font-size: 0.875rem; }
.commit-type code { min-width: 80px; }
.commit-type span { color: var(--color-text-secondary); }

.rating-table { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.75rem; margin: 1.5rem 0; }
.rating-row {
  display: flex; gap: 1.25rem; align-items: flex-start;
  padding: 1rem 1.1rem; border-radius: 8px;
  border: 1px solid rgba(119,141,169,0.15);
  background: rgba(65,90,119,0.12);
}
.rating-row strong { display: block; color: var(--color-text-primary); font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 0.3rem; }
.rating-row p { color: var(--color-text-secondary); font-size: 0.875rem; line-height: 1.55; margin: 0; }

.rating-badge-e, .rating-badge-t, .rating-badge-m {
  font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.75rem; font-weight: 700;
  padding: 0.25rem 0.6rem; border-radius: 4px; border: 1px solid;
  letter-spacing: 0.04em; flex-shrink: 0; margin-top: 2px; height: fit-content;
}
.rating-badge-e { background: rgba(128,237,153,0.15); color: #80ED99; border-color: rgba(128,237,153,0.3); }
.rating-badge-t { background: rgba(255,209,102,0.15); color: #FFD166; border-color: rgba(255,209,102,0.3); }
.rating-badge-m { background: rgba(255,107,107,0.15); color: #FF6B6B; border-color: rgba(255,107,107,0.3); }

.size-table { display: flex; flex-direction: column; border: 1px solid rgba(119,141,169,0.2); border-radius: 8px; overflow: hidden; margin: 1.5rem 0; }
.size-row {
  display: grid; grid-template-columns: 120px 80px 1fr;
  gap: 1rem; padding: 0.85rem 1rem;
  border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(119,141,169,0.1);
  align-items: center; font-size: 0.875rem;
}
.size-row:last-child { border-bottom: none; }
.size-label { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.75rem; color: var(--color-border); }
.size-value { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.95rem; color: var(--color-text-primary); font-weight: 600; }
.size-desc { color: var(--color-text-secondary); line-height: 1.5; }

.dont-list { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1rem; margin-top: 1rem; }
.dont-item { display: flex; gap: 1rem; padding: 1rem 1.25rem; border-radius: 8px; align-items: flex-start; }
.dont-item.danger { background: rgba(255,107,107,0.07); border: 1px solid rgba(255,107,107,0.2); }
.dont-item.warning { background: rgba(255,209,102,0.06); border: 1px solid rgba(255,209,102,0.15); }
.dont-label {
  font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.7rem; font-weight: 500;
  text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.1em;
  padding: 0.2rem 0.5rem; border-radius: 4px;
  flex-shrink: 0; margin-top: 2px; height: fit-content;
}
.dont-item.danger .dont-label { background: rgba(255,107,107,0.15); color: var(--color-danger); }
.dont-item.warning .dont-label { background: rgba(255,209,102,0.12); color: var(--color-accent); }
.dont-item p { margin-bottom: 0; font-size: 0.9rem; }

@media (max-width: 768px) {
  .docs-layout { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  .docs-sidebar { position: static; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(119,141,169,0.2); padding-bottom: 1.5rem; }
  .sidebar-nav ul { flex-direction: row; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.25rem; }
  .field-row { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 0.25rem; }
  .field-row.header { display: none; }
  .size-row { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; }
  .size-desc { grid-column: 1 / -1; }
}
</style>
